# A refusal that lists two of the three kinds it accepts sends the reader off
# to check the third by hand. `to_int` and `to_float` both take the bytes a
# file read hands back, and neither said so; both now name every kind they
# take, and name what arrived instead the way `length` has all along.
#
# The float arrives through a call because a literal one is refused before the
# program runs — `text/to_int 3.5` is the compile-time check doing its job, and
# this fixture is about the runtime path underneath it.
import "std/text"

fn measured 0
  3.5

pub play = print "{text/to_int (measured 0)}"
